id: pm-csv-import-custom-columns
title: Preserve registered custom columns in CSV imports
description: The legacy importer reads only the fixed built-in IMPORT_COLUMNS and rowFields schema. Custom columns emitted by export --all-fields are silently ignored on CLI re-import. Discovered while strengthening packed acceptance; SDK adapter re-import is separate evidence and does not certify CLI custom-field import.
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-26T08:23:24.402Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T09:07:08.370Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Resolve registered columns and metadata aliases through the SDK; preserve supported field types and empty values through CLI re-import; cover create, update, preview, stream and atomic paths with real tracker tests; reject invalid typed cells before mutation."
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T08:23:59.361Z",codex-agent,Follow-up from pm-csv-packed-custom-fields. The packed acceptance fixture roundtrip uses the SDK import adapter and must not be described as proof that the legacy CLI importer preserves custom columns.
  "2026-10-27T09:00:25.751Z",codex-agent,PR #202 proves SDK adapter round-trip and packed export only. Native CLI custom-column import across create/update/preview/stream/atomic paths and typed-cell validation remain undelivered; this issue stays open. Reviewed merged PR #202 (6350dc85597f9019a9148b1ac44221467546ed62).
  "2026-10-27T09:07:06.414Z",codex-agent,PR #202 proves SDK adapter round-trip and packed export only. Native CLI custom-column import across create/update/preview/stream/atomic paths and typed-cell validation remain undelivered; this issue stays open. Reviewed merged PR #202 (6350dc85597f9019a9148b1ac44221467546ed62).
files[1]{path,scope}:
